; A line the grammar does not recognise used to be skipped rather than
; reported, so only a line that *started* like a directive and then went wrong
; was ever an error. That is how a typo lives in a ledger for months.
;
; The catch-all now claims only the lines beancount itself ignores (see
; structure/org-mode-lines.beancount); anything else stops the parse.
